WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.110
- Former President, Trump,

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.850
has sued basically all of social media

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.500
for de-platforming him.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.430
He has sued Twitter, Facebook, and YouTube

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.650
claiming that they somehow
violated the first amendment

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.780
by kicking him off of their platforms.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.280
This is going to fail spectacularly.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.730
Number one, he filed as a class action.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:20.250
This is not a class action.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.330
Second of all, you, the viewer

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.910
seem to know more about section 230

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:26.320
of the Communications Decency Act

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.630
than former President
Trump and his lawyers.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.370
It doesn't do the things
that he says it does.

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:32.880
It's the first amendment that allows them

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.590
to kick him off of their
platform, it's not section 230.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.510
And this whole thing may be sanctionable.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.160
Former President Trump
filed suit in Florida

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.520
which has an anti-slap law.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.770
It's not a particularly
strong one, but it does exist.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.950
So this whole lawsuit may be
kicked out on an anti-slap.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.253
So we'll see if we see them in court.

